            "pk": "18111689248681230",
            "text": "🚀Asia as the New Venture Hub: How Startups from Kazakhstan Can Attract Investment and Enter Markets in China, Korea, Japan, and Southeast Asia.\n\nAsia is no longer an “alternative market” - it is one of the fastest-growing venture hubs where new rules are being shaped.\n\nIn this session, we will explore how startups from Kazakhstan can enter Asian ecosystems, attract investment, and build real deals - not just networking for the sake of networking.\n\n💫Speaker:\nJaeyeong Park, Co-founder of The Garrison (Seoul), works with international startups, helping them enter the Korean market and build partnerships with corporations and investors.\n\nModerator:\nDiana Bakbergenova - startup mentor, producer.\n\nWe’ll cover:\n— how venture markets in Asia actually work today\n— what investors in Korea, China, Japan, and Southeast Asia really look for\n— how to prepare your startup to enter these markets\n— common mistakes that prevent deals from happening\n— how to build cross-border partnerships and close deals\n\nThe session will be held in English.\nSeats are limited - registration required. \n\n📌Registration link is in the bio: @almaty.hub.02\n\n📅 MAY 8\n🕖 2:00 PM\n📍 Almaty Hub, Zenkov St. 24 (4th floor)"
